PART 2. FORKS AND DERIVATIVE WORKS - REVENUE SHARE

Any Licensee who creates a fork, derivative work, modification, port, wrapper, or substantially derived product (each a "Derivative") of the Software agrees, by the act of doing so, to the terms of this Part 2.

2.1 Prohibition on unauthorized monetization

No person may derive any direct or indirect financial benefit from a Derivative without a written commercial agreement with the Licensor. Authorization may not be presumed, implied, or obtained by conduct; it exists only upon a signed agreement.

2.2 Notification and agreement

Before any monetization of a Derivative, the Licensee must contact the Licensor at <typ.onepatop@gmail.com> and conclude a formal commercial agreement in writing. The Licensor may accept, reject, or condition any such request in its sole discretion.

2.3 Revenue share (minimum royalty)

The base royalty payable to the Licensor shall be no less than 50% (fifty percent) of the Derivative's Gross Revenue, unless a different rate is set by the written agreement. The Licensor may, at its sole discretion, permit a lower rate or waive the royalty for a specific licensee; such waiver binds the Licensor only in writing and only for the specific Derivative identified in the waiver. The minimum rate of 50% may not be altered by course of dealing, industry custom, or unilateral determination by the Licensee.

"Gross Revenue" means all revenue, income, payments, fees, subscriptions, commissions, advertising receipts, licensing fees, sponsorship, donations in exchange for features, and any other consideration of any kind, in cash or in kind, received by or accruing to the Licensee (and any affiliate, associate, or entity acting in concert with the Licensee) from or in connection with the Derivative, before any deductions whatsoever, including before taxes, expenses, costs, refunds, chargebacks and partner fees.

2.4 Accounting, payment and audit

(a) The Licensee shall account to the Licensor for Gross Revenue on a calendar-quarterly basis, in legible written form, within thirty (30) days of the end of each quarter.

(b) The royalty shall be paid within fourteen (14) days of each accounting statement, to the bank account or payment method designated by the Licensor.

(c) The Licensor, or its duly authorized agent, shall have the right, upon reasonable notice, to inspect, copy and audit the Licensee's books, records and accounts relating to the Derivative for a period of up to three (3) years after the end of each relevant accounting period. Any audit showing an underpayment of more than 5% (five percent) shall be at the Licensee's sole cost, and the shortfall plus interest shall be paid immediately.

2.5 Survival

The obligations of this Part 2 survive the termination of any license, the discontinuation of the Software, and the transfer or assignment of any rights or obligations by the Licensee, including through bankruptcy, liquidation or dissolution of the Licensee.

PART 3. BACK-FEED CLAUSE - AUTOMATIC ASSIGNMENT OF IMPROVEMENTS AND CONTRIBUTIONS (CLA)

To protect the integrity of the Software and prevent fragmentation of the codebase, this Part 3 imposes a mandatory, non-waivable back-feed of rights to the Licensor.

3.1 Automatic assignment of Improvements

All Improvements - meaning any and all modifications, enhancements, corrections, fixes, patches, optimizations, new features, modules, adaptations, translations, ports, and derivative works of any kind created by any Licensee based on, derived from, or in connection with the Software - are hereby automatically, irrevocably and without any payment or other compensation assigned to the Licensor as of the moment of their creation, to the fullest extent permitted by law. This assignment includes all copyright, database rights, and any other intellectual property rights capable of assignment, together with the exclusive right to sublicense, commercialize, register and enforce such rights in every territory.

3.2 Right of integration

The Licensor shall have the unconditional, perpetual and worldwide right to copy, import, merge, adapt and incorporate any Improvement published in any public repository (including forks hosted on GitHub or any other platform), and any code embodied therein, into the main development line of the Software and into any commercial or closed editions thereof, without any payment, attribution, notice or obligation of any kind to the creator of the Improvement.

3.3 Contributions - express assignment (CLA)

By submitting code to the Software's main repository through a pull request, patch, issue-fix, mailing list, forum or any other channel (a "Contribution"), the contributor represents, warrants and confirms that:

(a) the contributor is the sole author of the Contribution and owns all rights necessary to grant the rights herein;

(b) the Contribution was not obtained in violation of any third-party rights;

(c) to the fullest extent permitted by law, the contributor irrevocably and unconditionally assigns to the Licensor all present and future rights, title and interest in and to the Contribution, including all copyright and all rights of a similar nature, for use in any territory and by any means, with or without modification, in any form, in commercial and noncommercial contexts alike, and the right to sublicense these rights to any person. The contributor acknowledges that from the moment of submission the Licensor may use the Contribution without restriction, acknowledgment or compensation.

(d) to the extent that any moral rights in the Contribution cannot be assigned, the contributor irrevocably waives their enforcement against the Licensor and its licensees, to the maximum extent permitted by law.

3.4 Irrevocability and perpetuity

The assignments and waivers in this Part 3 are irrevocable, perpetual, worldwide and survive the termination of any license, the death or winding-up of a natural or legal Licensee, and any transfer of the Software to a successor in title.

